# Private working material — NEVER committed (this repo is public).
plan/

# Node
node_modules/
# npm lockfiles: deliberately not committed — every recipe pins `@cendor/*` RANGES so `npm install`
# re-resolves the current shipped minor on each CI run. Drift then shows up as a red job instead of
# being frozen into a lockfile nobody re-reads. (Same rule as the Python cookbook's uv.lock.)
package-lock.json
npm-debug.log*
.npm/

# Build output. Recipes are TypeScript-source (`index.mts`) with the runnable `index.mjs` GENERATED
# beside them and COMMITTED — that committed .mjs is a product, not build output, so it is not
# ignored. What is ignored: tsc bookkeeping and the scratch tree `build-recipes.mjs` formats in
# before comparing (normally removed at the end of a run; left behind only if one crashes).
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.recipe-build/

# Secrets & local config — recipes run offline with NO key; never commit one.
.env
*.env

# Cassettes recorded locally are generated artifacts, not fixtures. (Committed fixtures live under
# a recipe's own fixtures/ dir and are added explicitly.)
**/_recordings/

# Editor / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.log

# Audit chains written by the agent recipes' `serve.py` / `serve.mjs` when a reader drives them
# from the M365 Agents Playground. They are per-run evidence, not fixtures — and without this rule
# following the recipe's own runbook dirties the tree.
chain.jsonl
**/chain-*.jsonl

# LIVE provider recordings. The `RECORD=1` path in every `recipes/providers/*` recipe writes a real
# recorded exchange here — a MAINTAINER artifact, never a shipped fixture. The Python cookbook
# commits exactly four fixtures (the two judge cassettes and the pytest ones), all recorded against
# an offline FAKE and therefore deterministic; it commits ZERO provider fixtures, and neither do we.
# Two reasons: a live recording carries real model output into a public repo, and — measured
# 2026-08-01 — a cassette outlives the code that produced it, so a fixture recorded under a
# temporarily-broken build keeps replaying that breakage long after the code is fixed.
recipes/providers/*/fixtures/
